          "content": "Chapter – 5 Parallel and Intersecting Lines"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.214,
            0.25,
            0.233
          ],
          "content": "**Page No. 107**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.14,
            0.247,
            0.752,
            0.286
          ],
          "content": "？ **Can two straight lines intersect at more than one point? Ans:** No"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.141,
            0.296,
            0.706,
            0.333
          ],
          "content": "**What patterns do you observe among these angles? Ans:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.188,
            0.336,
            0.389,
            0.353
          ],
          "content": "∠a = ∠c and ∠b = ∠d."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.187,
            0.354,
            0.516,
            0.373
          ],
          "content": "∠a + ∠b = 180° and ∠b + ∠c = 180°."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.187,
            0.375,
            0.441,
            0.393
          ],
          "content": "Find more such relations."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.141,
            0.406,
            0.715,
            0.444
          ],
          "content": "**Is this always true for any pair of intersecting lines? Ans:** Yes"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.455,
            0.255,
            0.475
          ],
          "content": "**Page No. 108.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.491,
            0.315,
            0.51
          ],
          "content": "？ **Figure it Out**"
